--------------------------
Gitea runner Configuration
--------------------------

The runner must be registered with a Gitea instance before its service is
enabled. Get a registration token from the instance (site, organisation or
repository settings, Actions, Runners), then register as the service user from
its home directory, where the registration is stored:

```
su gitea-runner -c 'cd /var/<prefix>/gitea-runner && \
    <prefix>/gitea-runner/bin/gitea-runner register \
    --config /etc/<prefix>/gitea-runner/config.yaml \
    --instance https://gitea.example.com --token-file <file> \
    --name <name> --labels <label>:host --no-interactive'
svcadm enable ooce/application/gitea-runner
```

There is no container runtime on illumos: use labels of the form
`<label>:host`, so that jobs run directly on the host as the `gitea-runner`
user. The default labels refer to Docker images and cannot be served.
